# Schemas

Purpose:
  Canonical schemas for SDDRA artifacts. Defines the structure and
  validation rules for tasks, decisions, workflows, skills, gates,
  and modules.

Owns: ./

ReadOrder:
   1 @INDEX.sdd
   2 @task.sdd (task schema)
   3 @decision.sdd (decision schema)
   4 @workflow.sdd (workflow schema)
   5 @skill.sdd (skill schema)
   6 @gate.sdd (gate schema)
   7 @module.sdd (module schema)

Rules:
  [SC1] All .sdd files MUST conform to their schema.
  [SC2] Schemas are immutable unless explicitly versioned.
  [SC3] Schema changes require migration plan.

Navigation:
  Task: @task.sdd
  Subtask: @subtask.sdd
  Decision: @decision.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow.sdd
  Skill: @skill.sdd
  Gate: @gate.sdd
  Module: @module.sdd

State: +
  (Phase 155: added @subtask.sdd — smallest execution unit schema
   backing /sdd-next --subtask)
